# Doc style (master rule — inherited by every product)

Every in-scope product is understood the same way. Five artifacts make a repo
self-describing to humans and agents alike. Templates live in the hub under
`docs/agentic-templates/`; this rule is the single source of truth for the style
and is propagated into each submodule's `.cursor/rules/` by
`scripts/propagate-shared-rules.mjs`.

## The five required artifacts

1. **`catalog-info.yaml`** (repo root) — machine-readable spine, Backstage
   `Component` schema. Hand-maintained metadata: `spec.type`, `spec.lifecycle`,
   `spec.owner`, `spec.system` (product group from `hub/projects.yaml` tags),
   and `annotations` for `stack` / `deploy-target` / `status` / `docs`. The hub
   registry generator reads this into `docs/registry.json`, so keep it accurate.

2. **`AGENTS.md`** (repo root) — the **single source of truth** for agent and
   human onboarding: what the product is, how to run/test/build it, constraints,
   and where the deeper docs live. Everything an agent needs to work here starts
   in AGENTS.md.

3. **`CLAUDE.md`** (repo root) — a **stub that imports AGENTS.md**, not a second
   copy. Its body is `@AGENTS.md` (Claude Code import, resolution depth ≤ 5) plus
   only genuinely Claude-specific lines that don't belong in the shared AGENTS.md.
   Never duplicate onboarding prose between the two — AGENTS.md owns it.

4. **`docs/adr/NNNN-title.md`** — Architecture Decision Records (MADR-lite:
   Context / Decision / Consequences). One file per significant decision,
   zero-padded sequential number. Start from
   `docs/agentic-templates/adr/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md`.

5. **C4 diagram in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`** — at least a Container-level
   `C4Container` Mermaid block (renders on GitHub and in the org dashboard). Keep
   Context/Container as the default zoom; go deeper only when it earns its keep.

## Conventions

- **Diátaxis** organizes prose docs (tutorial / how-to / reference / explanation)
  as a guideline — don't force empty files, but sort content into the right mode.
- Prose lives under `docs/`; the five artifacts above are mandatory, the rest of
  the doc pack (SRS/TDD/PLAN/FEATURES/LEFTOVER_CHECKLIST) is governed by
  `docs-first-agentic` and `feature-registry`.
- When a decision changes an ADR's outcome, add a new ADR that supersedes it —
  never silently rewrite history.

## Exclusions

Same as the doc pack: `food-delivery-multivendor`, `erp-lite` (see
[`doc-pack-exclusions.mdc`](./doc-pack-exclusions.mdc)). These do not carry the
five artifacts and are skipped by the propagation script.

